Z||000000||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||04-28-2000||02:32 AM||||<BR>I just wanted to write this for the people that worry about buying a Fiero!  This is the board that people ask for help, not where they talk about how great the car is!  And it Is!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Mine is an '86 GT, with 5spd, and of course the V6.  It has 285,000 miles on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Everything is original, oil pressure is great, and looses NO oil in between oil changes (every 3500 miles).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The only things I (or my family, since my step-dad bought it Brand New) have done since new is:  2 clutches (one last month), clutch master cylinder, shift cables (3 times), heater core (3 weeks ago), brake pads (4 times),  Rear wheel bearings (yesterday), Shocks & Springs, Light bulbs, and Tires.   Now if this makes a car bad or unreliable, then I will bur a new car right now!     <p>[This message has been edited by Jeff's '86 1/2 GT (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||14
